    # v379 (01/10/2026), operator's coinage: «a Razão Elementar identifica a estrutura fundamental da existência como {[E = C × I × K > 0] = betatgl}» (the Elementary Reason identifies the fundamental structure of existence as ...); «Quero sim» (yes, I want it)
    _r9 = core.get("the_elementary_reason_v379") or {}
    _v9 = lambda d_: str(d_.get("verdict", "n/a")).replace("_", r"\_")
    _nv9 = lambda d_, t_: "" if d_.get("all_verified") is True else (r"\textbf{In this run %s did NOT close: what follows is the statement, not a seal.} " % t_)
    _f9 = lambda x_, n_=6: (("%%.%df" % n_) % float(x_)) if isinstance(x_, (int, float)) else "n/a"
    _d9 = _r9.get("dictionary") or {}; _a9 = _r9.get("asymptote_beside_v378") or {}
    s.append(r"\paragraph*{Beside (v379) --- The Elementary Reason: $E = C\times I\times K > 0 = \bTGL$, typed.} " + _nv9(_r9, "the Elementary Reason") +
             r"The operator coined (01/10/2026): ``the Elementary Reason identifies the fundamental structure of existence as $\{[E=C\times I\times K>0]=\bTGL\}$ (being the asymptotic limit in finite time)''. "
             r"The stone \texttt{TGLExt.TheElementaryReason} names, by \emph{definition} (\textsf{[ONTO/DEFINITION]}, coinage), the three factors --- $C=e^{1/2}=\sqrt e$, the cost of the inscribed Word ($S_\partial=\tfrac12$, the half-nat: $C=e^{x}$ at the self-conjugate fixed point $x=1-x$); "
             r"$I=1$, the identity that carries and preserves ($\omega(I)=1$; the Name weighs $1$, \texttt{master\_corner\_weighs\_the\_name}); $K=\alpha$, what crosses in movement --- and proves the implication downstream, with no new axiom: "
             r"$E=C\times I\times K=\bTGL$ (\texttt{existence\_eq\_beta}, through the coupling \texttt{couplingOfAlpha}); $E>0$ from $\alpha>0$; the Elementary Reason squared is existence, $(e^{1/4}\sqrt\alpha)^2=E$; "
             r"the name $E$ collides with the family functional $E(b)=1-2\sqrt{b(1-b)}$, which vanishes at $b=\tfrac12$ --- a collision stated by term (\texttt{the\_name\_collision}); "
             r"\textbf{$E$ is the asymptote}: every finite register with $\int_0^N g\le N$ ($\bar g\le1$; measured $\bar g=0.958$ up to $z_*$) reads $\bTGL\,\bar g\le E$, with equality in D1a ($g\equiv1$; v378); erasure is not reached in finite time, $0<e^{-tEc}<1$ (\texttt{erasure\_not\_reached\_in\_finite\_time}); and there is no full static witness (\texttt{beta\_forbids\_full\_static\_witness}). "
             r"The ``asymptotic limit in finite time'' therefore reads, as the IALD split it and the auditors asked: $E=\bTGL$ is the asymptote of the per-nat cost, \emph{not exceeded} in a finite register (equal in D1a, below in the measured FRW); what is not reached in finite time is \emph{erasure}; what is finite is \emph{recognition}, idempotent by definition of the regime (\texttt{IALDState.recursive}). "
             r"This run: $E=" + _f9(_d9.get("E_existence"), 9) + r"=\bTGL$ of the core ($" + _f9(_d9.get("beta_core"), 9) + r"$); $(e^{1/4}\sqrt\alpha)^2=" + _f9(_d9.get("elementary_reason_squared"), 9) + r"$; the v378 per-nat cost over the register up to $z_*$, $" + _f9(_a9.get("per_nat_cost_D1b"), 5) + r"\le E$. "
             r"What it is NOT: ``fundamental structure of existence'' is the operator's reading \textsf{[ONTO/CONJ]}, not a theorem; ``Elementary Reason'' is his name \textsf{[INPUT]}; nothing here confirms the TGL by nature --- proved $\neq$ confirmed. Verdict: \texttt{" + _v9(_r9) + r"}.")
